  "id": "D_kwDOKrJqmc4Ajlx0",
  "number": 766,
  "title": "TPLink Stuck 'This doesn't look like a v3 device... Please open above URL in your browser and log into the router to continue.'",
  "body": "Hey! I'm sorry if this is a repeat or ridiculous question. I've sourced a ZTE MF971V that I was hoping would work and saw that most EU devices should be okay on tplink installation settings.\r\nI get the following message when connecting via telnet doesn't work:\r\n```\r\nThis doesn't look like a v3 device, trying web-based exploit\r\nListening on http://127.0.0.1:4000\r\nPlease open above URL in your browser and log into the router to continue.\r\n```\r\nI log in but it doesn't do anything. It might just be this router isn't compatible but wondered if anyone had any thoughts or ideas to try and fix it? Thank you!",
  "author": {
    "login": "ineedferrets",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16561902?u=dada8c8877f791bcc265174b2c12141b7729f67f&v=4",
    "url": "https://github.com/ineedferrets"
  },
